[suggestion] The original name `containsUnsupportedFunction` seems reasonable. Can you revert the name and refactor the function body?

```js
const UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTIONS = new Set(['env']);

function containsUnsupportedFunction(cssTreeNode) {
	return Boolean(find(cssTreeNode, (node) => node.type === 'Function' && UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTIONS.has(node.name.toLowerCase())));
}
```

